SUMMARY:National Theatre Live: The Misanthrope @ WTW St Austell
DESCRIPTION:National Theatre Live: The Misanthrope (2h 30min)\n\nAward-winn
 er Sandra Oh (Killing Eve) plays the title role in this razor-sharp reimag
 ining of Molière classic dark comedy.\nTelling the truth isn't always tha
 t simple. Alice\, a brilliant novelist\, despises the carefully constructe
 d lies of modern society. But the more she challenges those around her\, t
 he fiercer the backlash becomes. Soon\, she must confront the price of spe
 aking her truth in a world that would rather silence her.\nFilmed live on
  stage at the National Theatre\, Indhu Rubasingham directs Martin Crimp's 
 (Cyrano de Bergerac) highly anticipated play.\n\nFilm release at WTW Cinem
 as St Austell\nBook tickets: https://wtwcinemas.co.uk/st-austell/film/5599
 /national-theatre-live-the-misanthrope\n\nFilm details: https://evenwebb.g
